<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav March industry output up 7.4 pct vs Feb.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav March industry output up 7.4 pct vs Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office</p>
<p>reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  MAR 97	FEB 97     MAR 96</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	    + 7.4	 +11.5	+ 5.0</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+ 9.2	 + 7.8	- 4.0</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)   104.5	  97.3	106.3</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO MAR)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+ 6.3	 + 4.8	+ 3.6</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)    98.4	 103.5	 90.1</p>
<p>NOTES -- March 1997 industry output was 54.5 percent below the same figure for 1991, before former Yugoslavia's breakup.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-March 1997 industry output was 55.9 percent below the same three-month period in 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
